Q: How do I change the color of VS Code’s selected file in the tab bar? A: <p>Use <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/api/references/theme-color" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>tab.activeBackground</code></a> and <code>tab.activeBorder</code> in your <code>workbench.colorCustomizations</code>. I'd avoid using <code>focusBorder</code> for this because it affects too many other elements.</p>
<p>Try this:</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>&quot;workbench.colorCustomizations&quot;: {
    &quot;tab.activeBackground&quot;: &quot;#ff0000&quot;,
    &quot;tab.activeBorder&quot;: &quot;#00ff00&quot;
}
</code></pre>
<p>The first one sets the tab background and the second handles the bottom border.</p>
